<Layout
  title={"Deterministic Null: A Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates"}
  description={"About: Pre-registered null-model control experiment testing where neural models exceed a zero-call 64-bit integer case loop across 4,030 drand-seeded instances."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Deterministic Null: A Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study builds and registers an explicit zero-model-call control arm (Shape D: a 64-bit integer loop over a verified append-only case store, implemented across Rust, Go, Python, C++20, and Julia) and measures the paired completion increment of frontier cloud and local open-weight language models against it under League of Entropy drand public beacons and OpenTimestamps Bitcoin Calendar receipts.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Cross-language determinism (Gate G2): five independent implementations (Rust, Go, Python, C++20, and Julia) agree bit-for-bit on the frozen conformance store digest (`0da4df8d9ccbce1e...`) and 1,000,000-record `DNULLMM1` `mmap` probe checksum (`15027705736`) with zero floating-point operations inside the loop and zero model calls at decision time.</li>
        <li>Pre-beacon cryptographic registration (Gate G1): two fixed-sample confirmatory runs — Track-A (`reg-exp-001`, 2,840 instances across modulo-6 to modulo-12 formal and SQLite families) and Track-B (`reg-exp-002`, 1,190 unique instances across Unique 3-SAT, Berkeley Function-Calling Leaderboard v3, Sierra tau-bench Retail, BigCodeBench v0.1.3, and SWE-bench Verified, plus 6 multi-file bug-fix repositories) — lock all store digests, prompts, sample sizes, and executor hashes before their target drand randomness rounds exist.</li>
        <li>Two empirical regimes separated by Good–Turing unseen mass: when structural feature cells saturate, frozen Shape D matches or approaches neural completion at zero decision-time model calls; on open compositional synthesis (unseen BigCodeBench tasks, unseen multi-file repositories, and unindexed surface idioms), neural substrates show large positive increments, while online crystallization amortizes recurring Zipfian traffic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: wall-plug or named-rail hardware joule meter readings (`board_metered = false`, `measured_j = None`; local Apple M5 Max counters are on-chip IOReport and kernel `ri_energy_nj` `reported_j` values, and closed-API server energy is recorded strictly as `not_available`), human third-party sealed Tier-3 task authoring, or that any shortfall of a finite store establishes model necessity.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/deterministic-null/dnull-control-protocol.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/deterministic-null/dnull-control-protocol.svg" alt="Four-stage Deterministic Null pre-beacon lock and paired evaluation protocol. Protocol diagram, not a hardware rail reading." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Pre-beacon registration (`Gate G1` + OpenTimestamps + `drand`) and paired evaluation protocol. Protocol diagram, not a rail power reading.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
